				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/thealienbaby" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4874276); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4874276&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608558959" alt="TheAlienBaby" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4874276)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/thealienbaby" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4874276); return false;" >TheAlienBaby</a></span> <span class="odate time_1608557379 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">21 Dec 2020 13:29</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13947341/men-are-expendable">Men Are Expendable</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4850155">
									

<p>Hey there Researcher Allied, I'll be briefly critting your idea today!<br />
Note that I am not an official reviewer (though I am a flight officer), so take everything I say with a grain of salt. WIth that being said, let's begin the crit!</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Open&nbsp;Crit&nbsp;+</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close&nbsp;-</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>So the biggest problem with the concept behind your anomaly is that it isn't actually anomalous. <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parthenogenesis#Humans">Human Parthenogenesis</a> (also known as human asexual reproduction) has been proven to be a viable reproductive option for humans. This is obviously a somewhat large problem (the concept behind your anomaly isn't actually anomalous), but for now I'll crit what else is there.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The SCP “steals” another woman's pregnancy in order to make the user pregnant, and children born this way might be “special”.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is a bit vague, but from what I'm getting this ritual will terminate another woman's pregnancy to activate the target's own pregnancy. Are there any ways of choosing which woman has their pregnancy stolen, or is it random?<br />
Also, this brings up a logistical problem: you say that the whole concept behind this anomaly is women reproducing without men, but how is this possible in a remote African village where methods of parthenogenesis aren't available? Basically, if the ritual requires the 'stealing' of another pregnancy, and there is no way to have asexual pregnancies in the setting, then wouldn't men be needed for this ritual for initial fertilisation, thus rendering the primary theme of this concept<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-454146-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-454146-1')">1</a></sup> null and void?<br />
ALSO also, what does 'special' mean in this context?</p>
<hr />
<p>I'd recommend brainstorming this concept some more and altering it, because it currently suffers from some crippling logistical problems that contradict its main theme.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
Anyway, that's it for my crit today. Thanks for reading, and I hope this helps!<br />
P.S Feel free to PM me once you've revised this concept as I'll be happy to recrit this. Please link this thread in the PM though, I don't want to have to go hunting through the forums to find your post.
<div class="footnotes-footer">
<div class="title">Footnotes</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-454146-1"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-454146-1')">1</a>. Men becoming obsolete due to women not requiring one for procreation.</div>
</div>

