<p>The Hapless Helper<br />
<strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Emotional/Mystery</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong><br />
Based on the Thumbling (Grimm Fairytale)<br />
- A tiny man the size of a thumb that seeks to help others.<br />
- It can inadvertently hinder those it tries to help.<br />
- SCP becomes pale and sickly if it cannot provide aid to others.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong></p>
<p>- SCP first appeared to keep a peasant family company.<br />
- It travelled the world, aiming to help, typically causing harm, but being legitimately helpful on several occasions.</p>
<p>- An example of a hindrance was when the SCP aiming to ‘help’ robbers burgling a cottage. It loudly performed the actions it was told, waking the residents.<br />
- The SCP left, assuming it helped the family when in actuality, it ended up causing the family to be shot after they tried confronting the robbers.</p>
<p>- Appeared and kept in contact with a girl it calls Allison who would later become an O5 council member.<br />
- After intense review, the SCP was allowed to accompany scientists and help within the site it is located at.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> Concise article with an interview log to explain the SCP’s connection to Alison.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I want to keep the focus of the article on the mysteries surrounding the SCP and its desire to connect with members of the Foundation. I generally want the article to feel like the SCP is a positive influence but with a slight hint of dread that something may go wrong in the future.</p>

							</div>

								
					
