<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Drama, History</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> i plan to use alot of interview style dialouges since the foundation primarily documents the entity through the locals who tell its story</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong><br />
•A Mountain range is really the site of a massive battle between giant stone entities<br />
•Local indian tribes allied with one entity and fought with it in the war with their magic<br />
•The mountain was wounded, the tribes had to sacrifice their magic to save it. leaving them vulnerable to european invasion.<br />
•The mountain has healed enough that the foundation has to appease the tribe to learn how to contain it, as having a literal mountain as an enemy is a problem.<br />
•The tribe ultimatley aim to aide the foundation but they seek to regain their magical abilities, an idea the foundation is uncomfortable with.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> chief mountain is originally a kainai story of a giant chief who laid down and became a mountain. this is a story told to outsiders and the real story is that the stoney chief was nearly killed in a great battle, and the surrounding mountain range is a graveyard of the battle in which the people tread over their corpses. the local tribes are &quot;keepers&quot; of the mountain and tasked with keeping it alive</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> a modern twist on a rare traditional indigenous story in order to help preserve one of my tribe's story, and to bring more indigenous stories besides the more well known bigfoot and wendigo.</p>
<p>**Additional Notes:*</p>

